{"availability":"available","full":"ecogetaway/oss-language-inclusion","name":"oss-language-inclusion","description":"Closing the localization gap in open source: evidence on how Indic and other under-served locales get reviewed upstream, plus i18n tooling — including i18n-security-lint, a CI scanner for defects in translated strings.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":6,"forks":1,"created":"2026-04-25T05:18:04Z","updated":"2026-10-09T10:37:55Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://oss-infrastructure-initiative.netlify.app/language-inclusion","topics":["bidi","ci","cldr","gettext","i18n","internationalization","linter","localization","localization-security","open-source","open-source-governance","plural-rules","security","software-supply-chain","static-analysis","translation","trojan-source","unicode","xliff","xss"],"demo":"https://oss-infrastructure-initiative.netlify.app/language-inclusion","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T07:13:35.763Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T07:13:35.763Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T07:13:35.763Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T11:08:00.481Z","stars":6,"forks":1},{"at":"2026-10-16T07:13:35.763Z","stars":6,"forks":1}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["From evidence base to shippable i18n infrastructure.","Provenance. Part of the OSS Infrastructure Initiative (Sanjay C. and Anirudh Raghavendra) — an evidence-first portfolio applying one method across three under-served open source contribution domains: internationalization, accessibility, and AI contribution. First published April 2026. Full portfolio under Companion Projects below.","Overview and related work: the Language inclusion workstream page on the OSS Infrastructure Initiative site, alongside the other workstreams. How the research is done: method and evidence rules."],"features":["Maintainers name the review gap themselves. Closing a Hindi localization pull reque